subject: fix(security): add SSRF guard to suggested-models + smartRouter (#3714)

CRITICAL: GET /api/providers/suggested-models accepts ?url= from query
params and fetches it server-side without validation — classic SSRF.

- Import and apply assertPublicUrlResolved in suggested-models/route.js
  before the fetch() call; return 400 if URL targets an internal host.
- Import and apply assertPublicUrlResolved in smartRouter.js getNodeModels
  before constructing the /models URL; skip node if baseUrl is internal.
  (MEDIUM: node.baseUrl is admin-configured but worth protecting against
  DB tampering / renamed node entries.)
- Add 6 tests in suggested-models-ssrf-guard.test.js covering loopback,
  cloud metadata (169.254.169.254), IPv6 loopback, private-network range,
  missing params, and public URL pass-through.
- Existing 15 tests in ssrf-guard-hardening.test.js continue to pass.
- Build syntax check: all 3 modified/added files pass --check.

False positives confirmed NOT fixed (by design):
- Deploy routes (cloudflare/vercel/deno): fetch(targetUrl) is inside
  string templates deployed as relay workers, not server-side.
- headroom/proxy: intentionally proxies to localhost, gated by dashboardGuard.
- cowork-mcp-registry: hardcoded REGISTRY_URL, not user-controlled.
- cowork-mcp-tools: already has assertPublicUrl.

